187 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (A Data Warehouse \(DWH\) is designed to efficiently integrate, cleanse, and structure data for reliable analytics and reporting. The process begins with raw data ingestion from multiple external and source systems, ensuring minimal load on core storage while maintaining scalability. The staging area serves as an intermediary layer where data is standardized, deduplicated, and transformed, enabling historical tracking through Slowly Changing Dimensions \(SCD2\). The 3NF layer ensures data normalization, reducing redundancy and preserving relational integrity. Finally, the dimensional layer restructures the data into a star schema, optimizing it for fast query performance, aggregations, and business intelligence applications. This structured approach enhances data accuracy, consistency, and accessibility, ensuring a high-performance analytical environment.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
