<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The DM layer plays a critical role in transforming raw transactional data into a structured format that is optimized for analysis, decision-making, and reporting. Unlike raw or normalized data, which may require multiple joins and transformations to extract meaningful insights, the DM structure ensures that data is pre-organized, pre-aggregated, and efficiently stored for analytical workloads.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
314 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Ultimately, the DM layer transforms complex transactional data into a well-structured, high-performance format, allowing businesses to gain insights quickly, accurately, and efficiently while maintaining a system that is scalable and easy to manage.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
