/Pg 18 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
316 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The logging system ensures data integrity, traceability, and efficient error handling by tracking the last successfully processed record to prevent duplicates and maintain incremental loads. Error handling captures failures and enables restartability, allowing retry from the exact failure point. Logging execution details like inserted rows, timestamps, and statuses improves auditability and supports debugging. Real-time monitoring helps quickly identify failed loads, reducing downtime and improving ETL reliability. Automated log cleanup prevents table bloat while retaining necessary historical data, ensuring a scalable and efficient logging framework.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
