345 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Incremental loading ensures that only new records are processed efficiently. The system first retrieves the latest processed timestamp from a materialized view, avoiding full table scans. Fact tables are partitioned by order_dt, reducing query time by scanning only relevant partitions. Indexes on foreign keys and date columns speed up joins and prevent duplicate inserts. The process uses ON CONFLICT or MERGE to insert new records while maintaining data integrity. To keep performance optimal, materialized views are refreshed, and old partitions are archived or dropped, ensuring efficient storage and query execution.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
